{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","characters":[{"id":"chr_tavi_reed","name":"Tavi Reed","role":"protagonist","description":"A junior Tide Warden raised among the Mangrove Terraces, Tavi learned to read waterlines from her grandmother before she could read a tide table. Now assigned to the Glassgate Locks, she has found the sills silting up far earlier than the survey predicts. She is slight and quick-moving, with a sun-browned face, close-cropped dark hair, and a habit of marking measurements on the cuff of her work coat. Her careful records have earned her respect among gate crews, but not yet the authority to challenge the guild calendar.","motivation":"Keep the lagoon's tide flowing for the whole city, especially the terrace families who depend on it for food and power.","goal":"Convince the guilds to pause the glassblowing season long enough for the gate crews to dredge the locks before the spring tide.","flaw":"She treats precise evidence as if it will persuade people on its own and hesitates to make a case in terms of what others stand to lose.","internal_conflict":"Tavi fears that speaking beyond her junior rank will make her seem reckless and discredit the measurements she trusts.","external_conflict":"The Glassblower Guild intends to keep its kilns firing, while the gates need to be shut and cleared before the spring tide; the silt rights dispute also threatens cooperation with the ferry crews.","arc":"Tavi starts convinced that accurate measurements should be enough to halt the firing season. When the Glassblower Guild challenges her survey at Bellmaker's Quay, she chooses to present the gate readings alongside a dredging plan that gives the ferry crews clear silt duties and terrace families a voice. By the end, she still relies on evidence but can also build a shared case and accept responsibility for leading it.","personality_traits":["observant","patient","earnest","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sill reading","description":"Measures water marks and sediment layers to identify changes in the locks before they show in the regular tide tables.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Tide-table analysis","description":"Compares seasonal tide records with current gate conditions to estimate when a lock will fail to pass enough water.","category":"technological"}],"home_location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","faction_id":"fac_tide_wardens"},{"id":"chr_sela_voss","name":"Sela Voss","role":"antagonist","description":"The elected kiln speaker of the Glassblower Guild, Sela grew up learning to shape lagoon glass at Bellmaker's Quay and took over the season calendar after her mentor's hands failed. She is broad-shouldered, wears a smoke-stained apron over bright woven sleeves, and keeps a small glass float polished in one pocket as a reminder of her first successful piece. She knows that every window and channel bell depends on guild craft, and she has spent years defending the workers' right to a reliable firing season.","motivation":"Protect the guild's livelihood and keep its skilled apprentices from being pushed into irregular, unpaid work.","goal":"Complete the planned long firing season before agreeing to any closure of the kilns.","flaw":"She equates compromise with surrender and uses the guild's charter to shut down discussion before alternatives are explored.","internal_conflict":"Sela knows the tide is essential to the city and fears that defending the season may make the guild responsible if the locks fail, but admitting that fear feels like betraying her workers.","external_conflict":"Tavi's early silting evidence calls for dredging before the spring tide, which would interrupt the guild's firing season and challenge Sela's authority at the quay.","arc":"Sela starts by refusing to let the kiln calendar be questioned. After Tavi shows her how a failed tide would strand both the kilns and the guild's deliveries, Sela must choose whether to keep invoking the charter or call a guild meeting to arrange a shorter firing window and a coordinated pause. She ends still protective of her workers, but willing to negotiate before the crisis forces the decision.","personality_traits":["proud","practical","protective","forceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Glass assessment","description":"Recognizes flaws in vitrified glasswork and can judge whether a lock panel or channel bell needs repair or recasting.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Guild negotiation","description":"Can organize artisans around a shared position and defend their interests in public meetings.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","faction_id":"fac_glassblower_guild"},{"id":"chr_oren_pell","name":"Oren Pell","role":"supporting","description":"A ferry cooperative dispatcher who grew up hauling reed stock and harvest between the Algae Fields and the Mangrove Terraces. Oren is lean and weathered, with a streak of silver through his black hair and a collection of tide-worn route tokens strung at his belt. He can keep a barge moving through a crowded channel by listening to its bells, and he knows how much work it takes to move dredged silt. Years of seeing the terraces receive the benefit while ferry crews carry the burden have made him wary of promises about the commons.","motivation":"Make sure the crews who dredge and transport silt receive fair recognition and the rights promised under the city's silt rule.","goal":"Secure a clear agreement that the cooperative can claim the fertile silt it dredges and that it will be spread on the terraces within the required season.","flaw":"He holds back help until every obligation is written down, even when delay puts the whole lagoon at risk.","internal_conflict":"Oren wants to protect his crews from being exploited, but worries that insisting on their claim will make them look selfish when the city needs them.","external_conflict":"The locks need urgent dredging, but the Tide Wardens and ferry crews disagree over who owns the silt and who will carry it to the terraces.","arc":"Oren starts by refusing to commit barges until the silt rights dispute is settled in full. When Tavi asks him to help clear the locks before the spring tide, he chooses to put crews on the first dredging run while publicly recording the silt and its destination under the existing rule. He ends willing to act before every dispute is resolved, without giving up his insistence on fair terms.","personality_traits":["wary","resourceful","fair-minded","dry-humored"],"abilities":[{"name":"Channel navigation","description":"Guides sail and paddle barges through the lagoon using channel bells, tide conditions, and knowledge of the routes.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Crew coordination","description":"Schedules ferry crews and cargo so dredged silt and harvest can be moved efficiently.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_algae_fields","faction_id":"fac_ferry_cooperative"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_tavi_sela","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_reed","target_character_id":"chr_sela_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tavi needs Sela to pause the guild's firing season, while Sela sees Tavi's urgent warning as a threat to her workers' livelihood and her authority."},{"id":"rel_sela_tavi","source_character_id":"chr_sela_voss","target_character_id":"chr_tavi_reed","relationship_type":"skeptical","description":"Sela doubts that Tavi's junior status and early measurements justify disrupting the kiln calendar, though she recognizes the stakes if the gate readings are right."},{"id":"rel_tavi_oren","source_character_id":"chr_tavi_reed","target_character_id":"chr_oren_pell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tavi needs Oren's barges and crews for dredging; Oren supports her warning but insists that the silt rights rule be honored."},{"id":"rel_oren_sela","source_character_id":"chr_oren_pell","target_character_id":"chr_sela_voss","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Oren and Sela compete over the timing and logistics of the firing season, as kiln demands constrain the ferry crews needed to move silt."}]}
