c_mist_rookery","faction_id":"fac_eel_school"},{"id":"chr_qiao_ming","name":"Qiao Ming","role":"supporting","description":"A Crane Sect covenant witness at Bannerhall, Qiao Ming has spent years recording challenges and preserving the terms of the First Banner pact. She is spare and upright, with a white streak through her dark hair and ink stains along the side of her hand. Her calm manner conceals an exacting memory for every broken promise and every properly witnessed duel.","motivation":"Keep the covenant credible enough that no sect can disguise an ambush as a formal duel.","goal":"Establish in public that Suyin's tally-stick was presented under the pact and obtain an envoy from each named sect.","flaw":"She relies on procedure even when its slow pace lets a dangerous feud worsen.","internal_conflict":"She fears that making an exception for a disowned student will weaken the covenant, but fears more that rigidly denying the tally will make its protections meaningless.","external_conflict":"The Crane Sect's authority is contested by the Eel School, and the sects are deadlocked over whether Suyin can invoke the tally-stick.","arc":"Qiao begins unwilling to recognize the tally-stick until its standing is clarified by the full covenant. After Keshan raises a formal challenge at Bannerhall, she must decide whether to let procedure become a pretext for delay; she instead records Suyin's presentation and the challenge in the same public ledger. By the end, she treats the covenant as a living obligation that must be witnessed and applied, not a rulebook that can wait out a crisis.","personality_traits":["precise","patient","stern","fair-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Covenant record","description":"Recites the terms and precedents of witnessed challenges and records them so disputes cannot be quietly recast.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_bannerhall","faction_id":"fac_crane_sect"},{"id":"chr_mai_ting","name":"Mai Ting","role":"supporting","description":"A Salt Warden responsible for safe conduct on Saltmarket Isle, Mai Ting learned to keep rival envoys talking through tense market days without letting neutrality become passivity. She is compact and quick-eyed, with a sun-faded scarf and a wooden tally board tucked into her belt. Her steady voice is more practiced at setting boundaries than smoothing tempers.","motivation":"Protect the market peace that allows families from rival schools to trade without fear.","goal":"Guarantee safe conduct for the envoys and host a meeting where all three sects can respond to the tally-stick.","flaw":"She is so determined to remain neutral that she sometimes delays naming an unfair threat.","internal_conflict":"She believes neutrality can preserve trust, but worries that silence in the face of coercion makes her an accomplice to it.","external_conflict":"Old memories of the Broken Challenge make envoys wary of meeting, while the dispute over the rookery threatens to spill into the market.","arc":"Mai begins by offering only routine safe conduct, hoping not to appear to favor Suyin or any sect. When Keshan's formal challenge risks turning the envoys' gathering into another contest of intimidation, she publicly sets market-peace terms and refuses passage to anyone who violates them. By the end, she understands that neutrality requires enforcing equal protections, and helps the envoys reach the moot without abandoning her impartial role.","personality_traits":["practical","watchful","diplomatic","resolute"],"abilities":[{"name":"Safe-conduct negotiation","description":"Sets clear meeting terms and wins agreement from envoys who depend on the Salt Wardens' market peace.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_saltmarket_isle","faction_id":"fac_salt_wardens"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_suyin_keshan","source_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_ren_keshan","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Lin Suyin and Ren Keshan clash over whether her tally-stick binds the Eel School and whether the rookery nesting ban can be respected while its fishing claim is heard."},{"id":"rel_keshan_suyin","source_character_id":"chr_ren_keshan","target_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Ren Keshan sees Lin Suyin's disputed authority as an obstacle to the Eel School's claim, but must address her through the witnessed challenge rules rather than ambush."},{"id":"rel_suyin_qiao","source_character_id":"chr_lin_suyin","target_character_id":"chr_qiao_ming","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Lin Suyin needs Qiao Ming to witness the tally-stick at Bannerhall; Qiao's support depends on Suyin accepting the covenant's public process."},{"id":"rel_mai_keshan","source_character_id":"chr_mai_ting","target_character_id":"chr_ren_keshan","relationship_type":"mediator","description":"Mai Ting guarantees Ren Keshan safe conduct on Saltmarket Isle while holding him to the same market-peace terms as every other envoy."}]}
