w requires making the truth public.","personality_traits":["observant","stubborn","protective","methodical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hull diagnostics","description":"Finds inconsistencies between a hull's declared status, load readings, and the practical signs of ongoing power use.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Sail rigging","description":"Can safely inspect and handle delicate sail assemblies within the limits of the logged heat budget.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_sela_nadir","name":"Sela Nadir","role":"supporting","description":"Sela Nadir is the Riggers' Union heat-roster keeper, responsible for the duty logs that govern every sunside shift. She joined the union after the Sail Fire, when a relative on a dock crew was injured, and has built her authority around making sure no supervisor can quietly stretch a worker's exposure. Lean, close-cropped, and usually carrying a slate inside a reflective sleeve, she knows which entries were made at the worksite and which were amended later from an office. She respects Mara's skill but distrusts her habit of carrying suspicions alone.","home_location_id":"loc_mirror_shed","faction_id":"fac_riggers_union","motivation":"Keep the safety charter enforceable and prevent the owners from using a crisis to weaken the union's control of heat rosters.","goal":"Show that the yard's duty records are intact and identify any shifts or maintenance windows that overlap the hidden hull's power draw.","flaw":"She clings to procedure even when a narrow exception could prevent greater harm.","internal_conflict":"She fears that bending a rule, even for a defensible reason, will give Helio Tank grounds to demand longer sunside shifts.","external_conflict":"Helio Tank is pressing for longer shifts, while Mara's investigation may require urgent inspection work that cannot ignore heat limits.","arc":"Sela starts by insisting that no investigation can proceed outside the roster, even when Mara's evidence is time-sensitive. After a power fluctuation threatens to erase a useful maintenance trace, she chooses to coordinate a properly logged, limited inspection instead of blocking it outright. She ends by using the heat records to support the case against the hidden hull and showing that safety procedure can expose abuse rather than merely restrain workers.","personality_traits":["precise","principled","wary","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Roster auditing","description":"Recognises altered duty entries and can reconstruct whether a work window complied with the safety charter.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Crew coordination","description":"Organises workers around a shared task while keeping assignments within logged heat limits.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_iven_tarek","name":"Iven Tarek","role":"supporting","description":"Iven Tarek is a maintenance electrician assigned to the Bastion Hulk, where the yard office and audit berth share limited power and instrument access. He was trained to maintain the old tanker-derived systems assembled during the Keel Year, and knows how improvised feeds can survive long after a hull is marked for disposal. He is soft-spoken, broad-shouldered, and keeps a grease-darkened set of circuit sketches folded inside his work jacket. A previous discrepancy in his section's records made him cautious about putting his name on any claim he cannot independently verify.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_charter_audit","motivation":"Keep the yard's electrical systems safe and avoid becoming the convenient culprit for someone else's unlogged work.","goal":"Trace the unexplained power draw to its source without compromising the audit instruments or falsifying a maintenance record.","flaw":"He avoids taking a position until he can prove every technical detail, allowing others to control the narrative.","internal_conflict":"His duty to the audit office conflicts with his suspicion that the consortium's interests are shaping what the office chooses to examine.","external_conflict":"Mara needs access to power records, but sharing them could expose Iven to accusations of leaking audit material or concealing a fault.","arc":"Iven begins by treating the live-hull reading as an instrument anomaly and keeping his concerns inside the audit berth. When Mara shows him a matching change in the service feed, he must choose between preserving his safe neutrality and allowing the record to be dismissed. He gives Sela and Mara a signed technical trace with its limitations clearly stated, ending as a cautious witness willing to distinguish uncertainty from silence.","personality_traits":["cautious","technical","reserved","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Power-system tracing","description":"Follows service loads through the yard's improvised electrical network and identifies likely sources of unexpected draw.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Instrument calibration","description":"Checks whether a reading is consistent with the instrument's condition and the surrounding system.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_acharya","name":"Ren Acharya","role":"antagonist","description":"Ren Acharya is the Helio Tank Consortium's charter representative at the Bastion Hulk, responsible for presenting the yard as compliant and profitable to the incoming auditors. Ren came up through salvage procurement and understands how a hull's value can be divided among contracts, spares, and scrap entries. Immaculately groomed even in the Bastion's worn workwear, Ren keeps a clean slate and speaks in the language of deadlines and liabilities. Ren believes the yard's survival depends on keeping its owners in control, even when that means using Shadow Dock and an incomplete mass ledger to preserve useful equipment.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Keep Helio Tank's charter secure and prevent the audit from exposing the consortium's handling of scrapped hulls.","goal":"Make the upcoming audit accept the recorded scrap totals before Mara can connect the live power draw to Shadow Dock.","flaw":"Ren mistakes control of records and deadlines for control of the truth.","internal_conflict":"Ren sees the hidden spare hull as necessary to keep the yard operating, but knows its unlogged status turns practical salvage into theft under the mass-ledger rule.","external_conflict":"Mara's evidence, Sela's heat records, and Iven's technical trace threaten to connect the hull to the consortium's decisions before the auditors finish their inspection.","arc":"Ren begins confident that the audit can be managed by limiting its scope and presenting the hidden hull as an accounting irregularity. When Mara's group assembles independent records that point to the same power draw, Ren must choose between ordering another concealment and admitting that the consortium kept the hull outside the ledger. Ren ultimately discloses the spare's existence to the auditors to prevent the crew from taking the blame, ending with the charter exposed to scrutiny and Ren's authority diminished.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","pragmatic","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract interpretation","description":"Understands how salvage, charter, and audit language affects the yard's obligations and liabilities.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Uses deadlines and competing interests to steer formal discussions toward a preferred outcome.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_sela","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_sela_nadir","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara relies on Sela to validate the heat and duty records, while Sela presses Mara to share evidence before it is complete; their different approaches create friction but strengthen the investigation."},{"id":"rel_mara_iven","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_iven_tarek","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara needs Iven's technical trace to prove the scrapped hull is drawing power, while Iven fears that helping her will make him a target in the audit."},{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ren_acharya","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara's effort to make the hull's live power draw visible threatens Ren's plan to have the auditors accept the scrap ledger as recorded."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_nadir","target_character_id":"chr_ren_acharya","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sela's enforcement of the union heat roster conflicts with Ren's support for longer sunside shifts, and the hidden hull investigation gives their dispute a concrete test."}]}
