 examine.","external_conflict":"Mara needs access to power records, but sharing them could expose Iven to accusations of leaking audit material or concealing a fault.","arc":"Iven begins by treating the live-hull reading as an instrument anomaly and keeping his concerns inside the audit berth. When Mara shows him a matching change in the service feed, he must choose between preserving his safe neutrality and allowing the record to be dismissed. He gives Sela and Mara a signed technical trace with its limitations clearly stated, ending as a cautious witness willing to distinguish uncertainty from silence.","personality_traits":["cautious","technical","reserved","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Power-system tracing","description":"Follows service loads through the yard's improvised electrical network and identifies likely sources of unexpected draw.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Instrument calibration","description":"Checks whether a reading is consistent with the instrument's condition and the surrounding system.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ren_acharya","name":"Ren Acharya","role":"antagonist","description":"Ren Acharya is the Helio Tank Consortium's charter representative at the Bastion Hulk, responsible for presenting the yard as compliant and profitable to the incoming auditors. Ren came up through salvage procurement and understands how a hull's value can be divided among contracts, spares, and scrap entries. Immaculately groomed even in the Bastion's worn workwear, Ren keeps a clean slate and speaks in the language of deadlines and liabilities. Ren believes the yard's survival depends on keeping its owners in control, even when that means using Shadow Dock and an incomplete mass ledger to preserve useful equipment.","home_location_id":"loc_bastion_hulk","faction_id":"fac_helio_tank","motivation":"Keep Helio Tank's charter secure and prevent the audit from exposing the consortium's handling of scrapped hulls.","goal":"Make the upcoming audit accept the recorded scrap totals before Mara can connect the live power draw to Shadow Dock.","flaw":"Ren mistakes control of records and deadlines for control of the truth.","internal_conflict":"Ren sees the hidden spare hull as necessary to keep the yard operating, but knows its unlogged status turns practical salvage into theft under the mass-ledger rule.","external_conflict":"Mara's evidence, Sela's heat records, and Iven's technical trace threaten to connect the hull to the consortium's decisions before the auditors finish their inspection.","arc":"Ren begins confident that the audit can be managed by limiting its scope and presenting the hidden hull as an accounting irregularity. When Mara's group assembles independent records that point to the same power draw, Ren must choose between ordering another concealment and admitting that the consortium kept the hull outside the ledger. Ren ultimately discloses the spare's existence to the auditors to prevent the crew from taking the blame, ending with the charter exposed to scrutiny and Ren's authority diminished.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","pragmatic","defensive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract interpretation","description":"Understands how salvage, charter, and audit language affects the yard's obligations and liabilities.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Negotiation","description":"Uses deadlines and competing interests to steer formal discussions toward a preferred outcome.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_sela","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_sela_nadir","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara relies on Sela to validate the heat and duty records, while Sela presses Mara to share evidence before it is complete; their different approaches create friction but strengthen the investigation."},{"id":"rel_mara_iven","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_iven_tarek","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Mara needs Iven's technical trace to prove the scrapped hull is drawing power, while Iven fears that helping her will make him a target in the audit."},{"id":"rel_mara_ren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_ren_acharya","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Mara's effort to make the hull's live power draw visible threatens Ren's plan to have the auditors accept the scrap ledger as recorded."},{"id":"rel_sela_ren","source_character_id":"chr_sela_nadir","target_character_id":"chr_ren_acharya","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Sela's enforcement of the union heat roster conflicts with Ren's support for longer sunside shifts, and the hidden hull investigation gives their dispute a concrete test."}]}
