d Tovin admits the old ledgers were concealed, Elin chooses to accept a witnessed partial allotment with a recorded return due at harvest. She ends still demanding accountability, but willing to make a shared route possible without surrendering her people's claim.","personality_traits":["patient","unyielding","observant","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Joins and tends orchard stock with careful handwork suited to recovering trees.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Soil reading","description":"Judges the condition of blight-ash plots by their texture, drainage, and growth.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families"},{"id":"chr_bera_noll","name":"Bera Noll","role":"supporting","description":"A veteran caravan guard and beast handler, Bera has carried seed stock across the routes since before the Millers' Split eased. She is lean, weather-browned, and walks with a stiff knee wrapped in a strip of old canvas; a hand-carved tally stick hangs beside her worn knife. She knows the Frost Gate's closing season from hard experience and has watched arguments over grain turn into years of separation. Her loyalty to Mara is real, but she thinks survival often requires leaving a dispute for another season.","motivation":"To get the caravan and its living cargo through the pass before winter isolates them.","goal":"Keep the caravan moving while preventing the feud from trapping it beyond the Frost Gate.","flaw":"She uses urgency to avoid conflicts that might be resolved if she stayed to hear them out.","internal_conflict":"Bera believes peace matters, yet doubts that people can settle old wrongs before weather forces a choice.","external_conflict":"The last frost is approaching while accusations and disputed grain threaten to delay the caravan between the towns and the high pass.","arc":"Bera begins measuring every disagreement against the closing pass and urges Mara to leave the market without reopening the records. When Elin's claim and the Cut Grain scandal threaten to strand the caravan, Bera chooses to spend a day's travel margin helping stage and guard the public stock comparison instead of forcing departure. She ends accepting that a short, deliberate delay can prevent a much longer winter of broken routes, while still helping the caravan reach the Frost Gate in time.","personality_traits":["stoic","resourceful","cautious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Beast handling","description":"Keeps pack animals steady and fit across difficult hand-led caravan journeys.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Weather judgment","description":"Reads seasonal signs and estimates when travel through the high pass will become unsafe.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_frost_gate","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell needs Tovin Reed's weigh-house records to establish what happened to the tithe, while Tovin's guarded defense of the Compact makes her suspect the ledgers are still being manipulated."},{"id":"rel_tovin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Tovin Reed sees Mara Vell's insistence on a public accounting as a threat to the Compact, but comes to rely on her willingness to test the grain rather than accuse him without evidence."},{"id":"rel_mara_elin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_elin_ash","relationship_type":"strained ally","description":"Mara Vell carries stock Elin Ash believes was promised to the Orchard Families; their dispute over the allotment pushes both to seek a witnessed settlement."},{"id":"rel_elin_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_elin_ash","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Elin Ash holds Tovin Reed res