[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_seedways","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A Seed Keeper entrusted with grading and carrying stock from Granary Hill, Mara is the granddaughter of a keeper whose name vanished from the caravan rolls after an accusation of adulterating seed. She has spent years proving her own exactness, keeping her dark hair braided beneath a patched wool hood and carrying a hand balance with a cracked wooden beam. Her caravan must cross the recovering towns before the last frost, but the forged tithe ledger and the Orchard Families' unpaid claim force her to decide whether strict procedure can still serve the people it was meant to protect.","motivation":"To preserve the seed stock and restore trust in the keeper's oath without repeating her family's disgrace.","goal":"Carry viable grain through Ford Market to the Ash Orchards and secure a fair settlement of the families' grafting-stock claim before the Frost Gate closes.","flaw":"She treats written procedure as safer than listening to people, especially when her own reputation is at stake.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that any compromise over the tithe will make her seem like the keeper her grandmother was accused of being.","external_conflict":"The Cut Grain scandal has put the Seed Keepers and Millers' Compact at odds, while the Orchard Families say the caravan is taking grain already owed to them.","arc":"Mara begins by believing that an unaltered ledger and a perfectly sealed measure are enough to prove her integrity. When the weigh-house records contradict the grain she has personally graded and the Orchard Families refuse to let the caravan pass without an accounting, she chooses to open the sealed tally with both parties present and compare it against the remaining stock. She ends willing to make her work answerable to the people who depend on it, even if that means sharing blame and risking her standing among the keepers.","personality_traits":["precise","watchful","reserved","steadfast"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seed grading","description":"Can sort viable seed from damaged grain by sight, touch, and careful sampling.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Caravan wayfinding","description":"Plans hand-and-beast travel between the valley towns with the last frost in mind.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_granary_hill","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers"},{"id":"chr_tovin_reed","name":"Tovin Reed","role":"supporting","description":"A Ford Market miller and keeper of the tithe ledgers, Tovin inherited a place in the Millers' Compact after the old route feud made every measure a political act. He is broad-shouldered, with flour worked into the creases of his hands and a repaired leather apron stitched with scraps from his father's mill sacks. He did not falsify the current ledger, but he has long protected the Compact by keeping its older records closed, including evidence that might explain why the routes split after the Millers' Split.","motivation":"To keep the market charter and the Compact from being blamed for a crime committed by someone else.","goal":"Find who diluted the tithe grain and prevent the scandal from reigniting the old route feud.","flaw":"He confuses protecting his community with withholding facts that could embarrass it.","internal_conflict":"Tovin wants the truth exposed but fears that the Compact will lose its charter and the town its leverage if its past mistakes become public.","external_conflict":"The Seed Keepers suspect the weigh-house, and the current false measure makes Tovin's ledgers look like a replay of the falsification that divided the routes for a generation.","arc":"Tovin starts by defending the Compact through silence, convinced that old records will only give its rivals ammunition. When Mara's open comparison of the sealed tally and grain shows that the current ledger cannot be trusted, he chooses to bring out the older route records and testify to the Compact's role in keeping them hidden. He ends prepared to face public scrutiny rather than let a fresh falsehood harden into another generation of suspicion.","personality_traits":["practical","proud","protective","wry"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger keeping","description":"Tracks measures, returns, and discrepancies across the market's tithe accounts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Weigh-house craft","description":"Recognizes faults in balances, measures, and the handling of grain sacks.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_ford_market","faction_id":"fac_millers_compact"},{"id":"chr_elin_ash","name":"Elin Ash","role":"supporting","description":"An Orchard Families planter who took up a plot in the blight-ash rows when safer land was scarce, Elin has spent years tending young trees and keeping a family record of every promised graft and measure. Her sleeves are patched at the elbows, her hair is silvering early, and ash-gray soil stains the hems of her work clothes. She is a patient grafter, but her patience has thinned as vault grain promised to the families seems to disappear into the caravan's accounts.","motivation":"To see the families who accepted the worst land treated as partners in recovery rather than recipients of charity.","goal":"Secure the promised grafting stock for the Ash Orchards and establish a dependable account of what the vaults owe.","flaw":"She holds grievances so tightly that she sometimes treats every delay as deliberate betrayal.","internal_conflict":"Elin wants to trust the seedway again, but fears that reconciliation will ask the families to forget the costs they already paid.","external_conflict":"The caravan's grain allocation appears to take stock promised to her people, and the approaching frost makes further delay a threat to the orchards' recovery.","arc":"Elin begins ready to block the caravan until it delivers the full promised share, certain that compromise will erase the families' claim. When Mara offers a public stock comparison and Tovin admits the old ledgers were concealed, Elin chooses to accept a witnessed partial allotment with a recorded return due at harvest. She ends still demanding accountability, but willing to make a shared route possible without surrendering her people's claim.","personality_traits":["patient","unyielding","observant","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grafting","description":"Joins and tends orchard stock with careful handwork suited to recovering trees.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Soil reading","description":"Judges the condition of blight-ash plots by their texture, drainage, and growth.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_ash_orchards","faction_id":"fac_orchard_families"},{"id":"chr_bera_noll","name":"Bera Noll","role":"supporting","description":"A veteran caravan guard and beast handler, Bera has carried seed stock across the routes since before the Millers' Split eased. She is lean, weather-browned, and walks with a stiff knee wrapped in a strip of old canvas; a hand-carved tally stick hangs beside her worn knife. She knows the Frost Gate's closing season from hard experience and has watched arguments over grain turn into years of separation. Her loyalty to Mara is real, but she thinks survival often requires leaving a dispute for another season.","motivation":"To get the caravan and its living cargo through the pass before winter isolates them.","goal":"Keep the caravan moving while preventing the feud from trapping it beyond the Frost Gate.","flaw":"She uses urgency to avoid conflicts that might be resolved if she stayed to hear them out.","internal_conflict":"Bera believes peace matters, yet doubts that people can settle old wrongs before weather forces a choice.","external_conflict":"The last frost is approaching while accusations and disputed grain threaten to delay the caravan between the towns and the high pass.","arc":"Bera begins measuring every disagreement against the closing pass and urges Mara to leave the market without reopening the records. When Elin's claim and the Cut Grain scandal threaten to strand the caravan, Bera chooses to spend a day's travel margin helping stage and guard the public stock comparison instead of forcing departure. She ends accepting that a short, deliberate delay can prevent a much longer winter of broken routes, while still helping the caravan reach the Frost Gate in time.","personality_traits":["stoic","resourceful","cautious","loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Beast handling","description":"Keeps pack animals steady and fit across difficult hand-led caravan journeys.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Weather judgment","description":"Reads seasonal signs and estimates when travel through the high pass will become unsafe.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_frost_gate","faction_id":"fac_seed_keepers"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell needs Tovin Reed's weigh-house records to establish what happened to the tithe, while Tovin's guarded defense of the Compact makes her suspect the ledgers are still being manipulated."},{"id":"rel_tovin_mara","source_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Tovin Reed sees Mara Vell's insistence on a public accounting as a threat to the Compact, but comes to rely on her willingness to test the grain rather than accuse him without evidence."},{"id":"rel_mara_elin","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_elin_ash","relationship_type":"strained ally","description":"Mara Vell carries stock Elin Ash believes was promised to the Orchard Families; their dispute over the allotment pushes both to seek a witnessed settlement."},{"id":"rel_elin_tovin","source_character_id":"chr_elin_ash","target_character_id":"chr_tovin_reed","relationship_type":"distrust","description":"Elin Ash holds Tovin Reed responsible for the market's unreliable accounts, while Tovin fears her anger will make any Compact concession seem like an admission of deliberate theft."},{"id":"rel_bera_mara","source_character_id":"chr_bera_noll","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Bera Noll has guided Mara Vell through earlier caravan journeys and urges her to weigh every attempt at reconciliation against the real danger of missing the last frost."}]}
</Output>
