oc_gate_of_receipts","personality_traits":["patient","plainspoken","wry","quietly resolute"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fare ledger","description":"Can recall the tolls he recorded and explain which entries were collected and which were waived.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nera_orrin","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_orrin_dask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nera Vell needs Orrin Dask's warrant and weigher's seal, while Orrin's insistence on formal proof makes her fear his caution will let the soul reach the scales too soon."},{"id":"rel_orrin_sella","source_character_id":"chr_orrin_dask","target_character_id":"chr_sella_ember","relationship_type":"institutional rivals","description":"Orrin Dask must issue the warrant that Sella Ember's Lamplighter Kin demand before opening the sealed ledger; each initially treats the other's office as the source of the delay."},{"id":"rel_nera_tavin","source_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tavin_rook","relationship_type":"advocate","description":"Nera Vell becomes Tavin Rook's advocate, while his direct account of the waived fares forces her to take responsibility for challenging the miscast entry."},{"id":"rel_sella_nera","source_character_id":"chr_sella_ember","target_character_id":"chr_nera_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sella Ember helps Nera Vell verify and seal the correction after the warrant arrives, balancing Nera's urgency with the archive's oath."}]}
