{"world_id":"wld_bellwether","characters":[{"id":"chr_iona_vell","name":"Iona Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"Iona is a bell-founder's apprentice raised among the furnaces and hammer echoes of Founder Row. Her late mother taught her to identify a bell by the smallest turn in its tone, and Iona wears her mother's brass name-token on a cord beneath her work coat. Soot freckles her pale cheeks, and her close-cropped hair is usually tied back with a strip of foundry cloth. She heard the impossible ninth pattern from the Sea-Wall Belfry and recognized a note that no mark in the Collegium's records could claim.","motivation":"Discover what is ringing the unmarked pattern before the Chiming reaches the city.","goal":"Trace the unfamiliar note to its source and persuade the founders and watch not to silence the storm-bells blindly.","flaw":"She treats her exceptional ear as proof that she alone can judge what others should risk.","internal_conflict":"She wants to honor her mother's careful craft, yet fears that obedience to the founders will let the city lose its names.","external_conflict":"The Parish Watch has ordered the bells stilled, while the Founder Collegium denies casting the bell whose note Iona heard.","arc":"Iona begins certain that hearing the pattern makes her responsible for solving it alone. When the watch moves to enforce its silencing writ at the Sea-Wall Belfry, she must trust broker Sella's dangerous testimony and share her evidence with the founders instead of withholding it to control the outcome. By the end, she accepts that her ear can reveal a danger but cannot decide the city's fate by itself, and she publicly stands behind a collective attempt to answer the pattern.","home_location_id":"loc_founder_row","faction_id":"fac_bell_founders","personality_traits":["observant","stubborn","precise","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tone reading","description":"Can distinguish a bell's casting and damage by subtle changes in its ring.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Foundry craft","description":"Knows how to inspect bronze, read a founder's mark, and assist with bell repair.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_aldren_mast","name":"Aldren Mast","role":"antagonist","description":"Aldren is a senior warden of the Parish Watch who carries writs up Bailiff's Stairs and enforces the silence laws. His older sister vanished during the nine-night fog remembered as the Lost Parish, leaving him with a deep suspicion of any sound that might draw the Chiming closer. He is square-shouldered, silver-haired, and keeps his uniform immaculate despite the damp; his name-token hangs visibly from a chain at his throat. He believes a still bell is a terrible but manageable risk, while an uncontrolled ring could cost the whole city its names.","motivation":"Prevent another fog catastrophe like the Lost Parish.","goal":"Enforce the order to still the storm-bells before the next fog arrives.","flaw":"He mistakes certainty and control for safety, even when the evidence is incomplete.","internal_conflict":"He fears that restraint will repeat the helplessness of his childhood, but doubts whether silencing the bells will leave the city defenseless.","external_conflict":"Iona's report of the pattern and the founders' refusal to silence the bells challenge his authority and the watch's writ.","arc":"Aldren begins convinced that enforcing the writ is the only responsible choice. When the approaching fog makes clear that the bells' strange pattern may be a warning rather than a threat, and Iona risks her standing to share what she has heard, he must choose between immediate obedience and listening to those who know the bells. He ends by suspending his demand for blind silence long enough for the founders to answer the pattern, accepting uncertainty instead of disguising it as control.","home_location_id":"loc_bailiffs_stairs","faction_id":"fac_parish_watch","personality_traits":["disciplined","grave","protective","unyielding"],"abilities":[{"name":"Writ enforcement","description":"Knows the watch's silence laws and can organize wardens to carry out a parish order.","category":"social"},{"name":"Fog discipline","description":"Keeps calm and communicates with signs when spoken names could be taken by the fog.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sella_quoin","name":"Sella Quoin","role":"supporting","description":"Sella is a licensed Fog Broker whose stall opens in the Fogmarket when fog gathers. She trades in names and secrets under the Brokers' Charter, keeping her own name-token hidden inside a leather sleeve and using a tally of small knots to track obligations. Once she sold a secret that helped the watch find a debtor, and the debtor's family has never forgiven her. Compact and sharp-eyed, she wears a waxed coat against the estuary damp and speaks with careful economy even when the market is quiet.","motivation":"Keep the Fog Brokers' charter from becoming an excuse for the watch to seize the market's trade.","goal":"Repay a name-debt connected to the strange bell pattern without exposing the people who trusted her.","flaw":"She turns every relationship into an account of favors owed, avoiding honest loyalty.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect the people bound to her debts but fears that giving anything freely will leave her powerless.","external_conflict":"The watch calls the brokers' name-debts extortion and may use its writ to shut down the Fogmarket; Iona needs Sella's knowledge to investigate the pattern.","arc":"Sella begins by offering Iona only information for a price, certain that a clean account is safer than trust. When the watch's effort to still the bells threatens both the market and the names she has pledged to protect, she gives Iona a crucial secret without demanding repayment. By the end, Sella still understands the danger of debt, but chooses to act from responsibility rather than keeping every bond transactional.","home_location_id":"loc_fogmarket","faction_id":"fac_fog_brokers","personality_traits":["shrewd","measured","wary","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market negotiation","description":"Can bargain over secrets and name-debts while navigating the Fogmarket's charter.","category":"social"},{"name":"Secret keeping","description":"Remembers the terms and connections behind complicated exchanges without speaking names in fog.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_beren_oss","name":"Beren Oss","role":"supporting","description":"Beren is the keeper of the Salt Chapel's registry, where every citizen's name is written on salt against the fog. He inherited the work from a succession of quiet custodians and has spent decades repairing smudged entries before the damp can erase them. Thin and stooped, with salt-white brows and ink stains on his cuffs, he carries a little wooden scoop for tending the registry. His own name is meticulously recorded, but he rarely speaks it aloud outside the chapel.","motivation":"Keep the registry intact so no citizen becomes unregistered and forfeit to the fog.","goal":"Determine whether the bell pattern has affected the salt records before the next fog.","flaw":"He clings to preservation so tightly that he delays necessary action until damage is undeniable.","internal_conflict":"He believes records can protect a community, yet knows the Lost Parish began with names that the registry could not save.","external_conflict":"The approaching fog threatens the salt entries, while the watch's order to silence the bells risks removing the city's defense before the registry can be checked.","arc":"Beren begins by guarding the registry and refusing to expose its fragile entries to anyone's investigation. When he finds that the strange pattern coincides with fresh disturbance in the salt records, he chooses to let Iona and Sella examine the relevant entries rather than preserve his secrecy at the cost of the city's warning. He ends still devoted to careful record-keeping, but willing to treat the registry as evidence for living people, not an object to protect for its own sake.","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","personality_traits":["patient","cautious","conscientious","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Registry keeping","description":"Can maintain the salt-written names and identify entries disturbed by damp or handling.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Historical memory","description":"Knows the chapel's records and the civic customs founded after the Lost Parish.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_iona_aldren","source_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","target_character_id":"chr_aldren_mast","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Iona Vell opposes Aldren Mast's order to silence the storm-bells, while Aldren sees her insistence on investigating the pattern as a danger to the city."},{"id":"rel_aldren_iona","source_character_id":"chr_aldren_mast","target_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","relationship_type":"authority conflict","description":"Aldren Mast holds the watch's authority over Iona Vell, whose evidence could force him to reconsider the silencing writ."},{"id":"rel_iona_sella","source_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quoin","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Iona Vell needs Sella Quoin's market knowledge, but Sella's habit of pricing secrets makes Iona doubt the broker's motives."},{"id":"rel_sella_beren","source_character_id":"chr_sella_quoin","target_character_id":"chr_beren_oss","relationship_type":"debtor","description":"Sella Quoin owes Beren Oss a name-debt tied to a secret she traded, and Beren's careful record of the obligation keeps their trust fragile."},{"id":"rel_beren_iona","source_character_id":"chr_beren_oss","target_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","relationship_type":"reluctant ally","description":"Beren Oss initially withholds the salt registry from Iona Vell, but the bell pattern's possible trace in the entries gives them a shared purpose."}]}
