_fog_brokers","personality_traits":["shrewd","measured","wary","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Market negotiation","description":"Can bargain over secrets and name-debts while navigating the Fogmarket's charter.","category":"social"},{"name":"Secret keeping","description":"Remembers the terms and connections behind complicated exchanges without speaking names in fog.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_beren_oss","name":"Beren Oss","role":"supporting","description":"Beren is the keeper of the Salt Chapel's registry, where every citizen's name is written on salt against the fog. He inherited the work from a succession of quiet custodians and has spent decades repairing smudged entries before the damp can erase them. Thin and stooped, with salt-white brows and ink stains on his cuffs, he carries a little wooden scoop for tending the registry. His own name is meticulously recorded, but he rarely speaks it aloud outside the chapel.","motivation":"Keep the registry intact so no citizen becomes unregistered and forfeit to the fog.","goal":"Determine whether the bell pattern has affected the salt records before the next fog.","flaw":"He clings to preservation so tightly that he delays necessary action until damage is undeniable.","internal_conflict":"He believes records can protect a community, yet knows the Lost Parish began with names that the registry could not save.","external_conflict":"The approaching fog threatens the salt entries, while the watch's order to silence the bells risks removing the city's defense before the registry can be checked.","arc":"Beren begins by guarding the registry and refusing to expose its fragile entries to anyone's investigation. When he finds that the strange pattern coincides with fresh disturbance in the salt records, he chooses to let Iona and Sella examine the relevant entries rather than preserve his secrecy at the cost of the city's warning. He ends still devoted to careful record-keeping, but willing to treat the registry as evidence for living people, not an object to protect for its own sake.","home_location_id":"loc_salt_chapel","personality_traits":["patient","cautious","conscientious","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Registry keeping","description":"Can maintain the salt-written names and identify entries disturbed by damp or handling.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Historical memory","description":"Knows the chapel's records and the civic customs founded after the Lost Parish.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_iona_aldren","source_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","target_character_id":"chr_aldren_mast","relationship_type":"opponent","description":"Iona Vell opposes Aldren Mast's order to silence the storm-bells, while Aldren sees her insistence on investigating the pattern as a danger to the city."},{"id":"rel_aldren_iona","source_character_id":"chr_aldren_mast","target_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","relationship_type":"authority conflict","description":"Aldren Mast holds the watch's authority over Iona Vell, whose evidence could force him to reconsider the silencing writ."},{"id":"rel_iona_sella","source_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","target_character_id":"chr_sella_quoin","relationship_type":"uneasy ally","description":"Iona Vell needs Sella Quoin's market knowledge, but Sella's habit of pricing secrets makes Iona doubt the broker's motives."},{"id":"rel_sella_beren","source_character_id":"chr_sella_quoin","target_character_id":"chr_beren_oss","relationship_type":"debtor","description":"Sella Quoin owes Beren Oss a name-debt tied to a secret she traded, and Beren's careful record of the obligation keeps their trust fragile."},{"id":"rel_beren_iona","source_character_id":"chr_beren_oss","target_character_id":"chr_iona_vell","relationship_type":"reluctant ally","description":"Beren Oss initially withholds the salt registry from Iona Vell, but the bell pattern's possible trace in the entries gives them a shared purpose."}]}
