{"world_id":"wld_thistledown","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_thistle","name":"Mara Thistle","role":"protagonist","description":"A hedge-witch and tea merchant descended from the family that forfeited the Ninth Stall. Mara learned her craft from recipes and small garden charms passed down through her family, but she has spent years selling from borrowed space rather than making a claim on the fair. She wears a patched green coat with dried herbs tucked into its pockets, and carries a brass kettle polished smooth by use.","motivation":"Restore her family's place in the fair without repeating the broken promise that cost them the stall.","goal":"Claim the Ninth Stall before the third bell of closing day by presenting a fair bargain and proving her tea trade can serve the fair.","flaw":"She tries to manage every obligation alone, believing that asking for help risks making another promise she cannot keep.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that her family's old failure means she is not fit to hold the stall, even as she resents being judged by it.","external_conflict":"The Carter Kin are quietly selling the Ninth Stall's lease, and Mara must establish her family's claim with the Tallykeepers before closing day.","arc":"Mara begins the fair determined to win the stall through solitary effort and hide her uncertainty. When the Tallykeepers' wishing tags show that her plan depends on more favors than she can keep before the third bell, she chooses to ask Juniper and Nella for a limited, clearly recorded bargain instead. She ends the fair willing to share responsibility and ready to claim the stall on terms she can honor.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","personality_traits":["observant","resourceful","reserved","warm-hearted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hedge infusion","description":"She coaxes gentle warmth and a faint calming fragrance from common herbs when brewing tea.","category":"supernatural"},{"name":"Tea blending","description":"She can balance unfamiliar samples into distinctive blends and remembers the ingredients by scent.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_wain","name":"Oren Wain","role":"supporting","description":"A careful representative of the Carter Kin, Oren handles the practical business of moving wains and arranging fair leases. He grew up hearing that a promise left hanging can burden an entire family, and he treats uncertain claims as risks to be settled promptly. His tidy brown waistcoat has a ledger pocket sewn inside, and a small brass wheel charm hangs from his collar.","motivation":"Keep the Carter Kin's dealings clear and prevent unresolved claims from following the fair from field to field.","goal":"Complete a sale of the Ninth Stall's lease on terms the Carter Kin can defend to the Stallholders' Round.","flaw":"He values a clean transaction so highly that he mistakes speed and certainty for fairness.","internal_conflict":"Oren wants to honor the Carter Kin's responsibilities, but worries that reopening an old claim will make every settled lease seem uncertain.","external_conflict":"Mara's family still holds a claim to the Ninth Stall, while Oren is trying to sell its lease before the fair folds its lanes.","arc":"Oren begins convinced that selling the lease quickly is the fairest way to resolve the Ninth Claim. When Mara presents her family's claim at the Wishing Barn and asks for a recorded contest rather than a rushed sale, he must choose between closing the deal and allowing the Tallykeepers to judge it. He agrees to pause the sale until the ruling, ending the fair more willing to treat careful reconsideration as part of keeping faith.","home_location_id":"loc_leap_lane","faction_id":"fac_carters","personality_traits":["methodical","practical","cautious","dutiful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Route memory","description":"He remembers the fair's changing lanes and the sequence in which the Carter Kin move its wains.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Terms keeper","description":"He spots ambiguous wording in a bargain and can restate it in plain, measurable terms.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_quill","name":"Tamsin Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A Tallykeeper who records promises on wishing tags and helps settle disputes of debt. Tamsin takes pride in making the rules legible to everyone, not just seasoned merchants, and has learned that a neat record can still conceal an unworkable bargain. She wears a russet apron with a row of blank tags and keeps her ink in a squat blue bottle.","motivation":"Make sure every favor is recorded clearly and judged by the same fair process.","goal":"Rule on the Ninth Stall claim and the fair's unsettled favors before closing day without allowing either side to rush the record.","flaw":"She can rely so heavily on written terms that she overlooks what people are afraid to say aloud.","internal_conflict":"Tamsin believes impartiality requires distance, but suspects her formality sometimes keeps people from bringing forward the truth behind a promise.","external_conflict":"The favour shortage leaves more debts outstanding than can be kept before closing, while Tamsin must judge disputes including the Ninth Stall claim.","arc":"Tamsin begins by treating every dispute as a matter of matching tags to terms. When Mara's claim and Oren's proposed sale meet at the Wishing Barn, Tamsin sees that the old record does not explain what each side can reasonably keep before closing. She invites both to state their terms before the Stallholders' Round and records a bounded bargain they can fulfill, ending more attentive to the people behind each tag while preserving the Tallykeepers' impartial role.","home_location_id":"loc_wishing_barn","faction_id":"fac_tallykeepers","personality_traits":["precise","patient","fair-minded","quietly curious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Promise ledger","description":"She can trace a favor's recorded terms and identify which promises remain unkept.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Calm mediation","description":"She helps disputants separate what was promised from what each hoped would happen.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_juniper_moss","name":"Juniper Moss","role":"supporting","description":"A tea-tent merchant in the Stallholders' Round, Juniper is known for generous samples and a talent for remembering customers' favorite cups. She has traded at the Kettle Commons for several leap-seasons and has seen how quickly friendly favors can pile up. Her sleeves are often dusted with spice, and she ties her dark curls back with a strip of saffron cloth.","motivation":"Keep the tea merchants connected without letting goodwill become a burden no one can repay.","goal":"Help the Kettle Commons settle its outstanding favors in time for the fair's closing.","flaw":"She offers help before checking whether she has the time or goods to provide it.","internal_conflict":"Juniper wants to be the person others can count on, but fears that saying no will make her seem ungenerous.","external_conflict":"The favour shortage threatens to leave several of her own tea-trade promises unkept before the lanes fold.","arc":"Juniper begins the fair accepting every request for samples and help, adding to the favors she already owes. When Mara asks her to support a recorded bargain at the Wishing Barn, Juniper admits which promises she can actually fulfill and offers a limited tea-supply pledge instead of another open-ended favor. She ends the fair still generous, but clearer about the limits that make her help dependable.","home_location_id":"loc_kettle_commons","faction_id":"fac_stallholders","personality_traits":["sociable","generous","quick-witted","overcommitted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sample host","description":"She can turn a tasting into a friendly conversation where merchants discover useful trades.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_nella_wain","name":"Nella Wain","role":"supporting","description":"A young member of the Carter Kin who helps tend the wains along Leap Lane and knows the fair's customs from listening to family stories. Nella is curious about how merchants make their living and is less certain than Oren that every old arrangement should stay untouched. She wears a sturdy blue scarf pinned with a wooden tag and keeps a small notebook of things she wants to ask.","motivation":"Help her family keep its promises while understanding the people affected by its decisions.","goal":"Find a way for the Carter Kin to resolve the Ninth Stall claim without leaving the fair with another unkept favor.","flaw":"She waits for someone older to speak first, even when she has useful information to contribute.","internal_conflict":"Nella respects her family's judgment but worries that silence makes her complicit when a decision is rushed.","external_conflict":"Oren's attempt to sell the Ninth Stall lease is moving ahead while Mara's family still holds a claim and closing day approaches.","arc":"Nella begins by keeping her doubts to herself while Oren arranges the sale. When the dispute reaches the Wishing Barn, she chooses to tell Oren that the Carter Kin can afford to pause the transaction long enough for the Tallykeepers to hear Mara's claim. Her intervention helps make a recorded bargain possible, and she ends the fair more willing to speak up within her family rather than waiting for certainty.","home_location_id":"loc_leap_lane","faction_id":"fac_carters","personality_traits":["curious","thoughtful","loyal","hesitant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Fair custom memory","description":"She remembers the customs her family has taught her about wains, leases, and promises at the fair.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_oren","source_character_id":"chr_mara_thistle","target_character_id":"chr_oren_wain","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Thistle contests Oren Wain's attempt to sell the Ninth Stall lease, while Oren questions whether her family's old claim can be resolved before closing."},{"id"