nticate registered star-maps and explain the safeguards governing their opening.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Institutional memory","description":"Knows the precedents and stakes behind the guild's sealing authority since the Map Wars.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_veska_dorn","name":"Veska Dorn","role":"supporting","description":"An Ice Baron who buys claims and tether rights ahead of each burn, Veska treats arbitration as another market in which timing matters more than sentiment. She has offered to fund Tovan's claim in exchange for future access to the route, though she frames the bargain as a way to keep indebted pilots from being stranded. Compact and silver-haired, she dresses in a dark mining coat with a tally of acquired claims stitched inside one cuff.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"Turn the uncertainty before perihelion into enough secured claims to keep her holdings viable through the burn.","goal":"Gain leverage over the perihelion route and acquire tether rights from pilots unable to pay their ice-tithes.","flaw":"She reduces people and promises to assets, assuming a favorable contract can excuse the pressure behind it.","internal_conflict":"Veska wants to see herself as a steward of the comet's scarce resources, but her bargains often deepen the very dependence she claims to manage.","external_conflict":"The Tether Grab has made the Free Pilots' Compact wary of the Ice Barons, and her support for Tovan could be exposed as an attempt to profit from the chart dispute.","arc":"Veska begins believing that buying claims is simply what keeps the market orderly before a burn. When Mara's hearing connects her proposed route bargain to the pilots' lost tether rights, Veska must choose whether to press the deal or withdraw it publicly. She withdraws the offer in the Long Hall, ending with fewer immediate gains but a clearer boundary between investment and coercion.","personality_traits":["Pragmatic","Composed","Shrewd","Possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim valuation","description":"Quickly estimates the risks and leverage in ice claims, berth rights, and pre-burn contracts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hard bargaining","description":"Can negotiate complex exchanges while keeping her own concessions difficult to read.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reik","relationship_type":"arbiter and claimant","description":"Mara must judge Tovan's salvage claim; his candor or evasion can determine whether she sees him as a pilot defending a right or a trader exploiting a theft."},{"id":"rel_serit_mara","source_character_id":"chr_serit_oss","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"guild superior","description":"Serit trained Mara in registration work and expects her to protect the Mapmakers' Guild, creating pressure when Mara's audit complicates the guild's preferred ruling."},{"id":"rel_tovan_veska","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_reik","target_character_id":"chr_veska_dorn","relationship_type":"uneasy allies","description":"Veska offers backing for Tovan's claim in return for route access, while Tovan suspects her support is a way to acquire influence over the pilots' tethers."},{"id":"rel_serit_veska","source_character_id":"chr_serit_oss","target_character_id":"chr_veska_dorn","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Serit sees Veska's claims-and-tethers strategy as a threat to a stable fleet, while Veska views the guild's control of sealed routes as a barrier to commerce."}]}
