{"world_id":"wld_comet_market","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A guild factotum assigned to keep the Map House's seals, registers, and hearing records in order, Mara grew up among berth ledgers at the Tether Docks before earning a place with the Mapmakers' Guild. She knows the burn articles by heart but has spent her career avoiding the consequences of applying them to powerful people. She is lean, close-cropped, and usually wears a slate-blue guild coat with ink-stained cuffs and a brass seal-counter at her belt.","home_location_id":"loc_map_house","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"Prove that the guild's rules can protect ordinary pilots as well as its own authority.","goal":"Determine who stole and resold the sealed perihelion map, then bring the dispute to a lawful resolution before the burn.","flaw":"She mistakes perfect procedure for impartial justice and delays hard choices while searching for a rule that will make them painless.","internal_conflict":"Mara wants to believe the guild deserves its authority, but the map's theft exposes how easily procedure can serve the powerful.","external_conflict":"The Mapmakers' Guild demands a piracy ruling, while the pilot holding the map claims salvage and the perihelion deadline leaves little time for a fair hearing.","arc":"Mara begins by treating the register as more trustworthy than the people named in it. When the hearing reveals that the map's sealed chain of custody cannot settle the pilot's salvage claim, she chooses to hear testimony from both sides rather than deliver the guild's preferred verdict. She ends willing to risk her standing by using her authority to make the Long Hall's ruling answer to evidence, not affiliation.","personality_traits":["Meticulous","Dry-witted","Patient","Conflict-avoidant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Seal and ledger audit","description":"Can spot inconsistencies in map registrations, custody records, and guild accounts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hearing craft","description":"Keeps contentious testimony focused on claims that can be tested under the burn articles.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tovan_reik","name":"Tovan Reik","role":"supporting","description":"A Free Pilots' Compact route-runner, Tovan took possession of the stolen sealed chart after finding it among disputed cargo at the Tether Docks. He calls it salvage because he believes the guild's exclusive control of routes has repeatedly endangered pilots, but he has not been honest about how quickly he tried to resell it. Sun-browned and broad-shouldered, he wears a patched flight harness and keeps a coil of tether line looped over one shoulder.","home_location_id":"loc_tether_docks","faction_id":"fac_free_pilots","motivation":"Make sure pilots keep a voice in deciding which routes they risk their lives flying.","goal":"Secure recognition of his salvage claim and prevent the guild from using the theft to revoke the Compact's arbitration rights.","flaw":"He treats every negotiation as a contest and hides inconvenient facts until trust is nearly impossible.","internal_conflict":"Tovan wants to defend the Compact's independence, yet his quick attempt to profit from the chart makes him fear he has become another opportunist using pilots as cover.","external_conflict":"The Mapmakers' Guild calls him a thief, and the perihelion route chart could be opened only by its sealer or the Long Hall arbiter.","arc":"Tovan begins convinced that withholding details is the only way to keep the guild from taking the chart. When Mara gives him a hearing instead of an immediate piracy judgment, he must choose whether to disclose the attempted resale that weakens his claim. He admits it before the Long Hall, ending the dispute with less leverage but a more defensible case for pilot representation.","personality_traits":["Daring","Suspicious","Charismatic","Impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Tether piloting","description":"Can maneuver a ship around the comet's slow spin using sails, tethers, and reaction plumes.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Route memory","description":"Recalls practical hazards and drift patterns from routes he has flown.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_serit_oss","name":"Serit Oss","role":"antagonist","description":"The senior sealer at the Map House, Serit inherited a reputation for exacting work after the Map Wars and has spent years defending the guild's right to seal every route. She insists that a stolen chart threatens the whole fleet, not merely the guild's prestige. Tall and severe, she wears a pale ice-fiber mantle fastened with a registry token and keeps her hands bare so no one can miss their fine, ink-dark seal marks.","home_location_id":"loc_map_house","faction_id":"fac_mapmakers","motivation":"Prevent unverified routes from sending ships into danger during the perihelion burn.","goal":"Recover the chart and secure a ruling that preserves the guild's exclusive sealing authority.","flaw":"She equates control with safety and dismisses any challenge to guild authority as reckless self-interest.","internal_conflict":"Serit knows the guild won its authority after the Map Wars nearly wrecked the fleet, but fears that admitting its limits will make that sacrifice seem meaningless.","external_conflict":"Tovan's salvage claim and the Compact's established arbitration rights threaten to turn the stolen chart into a public challenge to the Mapmakers' Guild.","arc":"Serit begins determined to make the theft a simple piracy case. When Mara's audit shows that the register can establish a seal but cannot prove the chart's later custody, Serit must choose between suppressing that distinction and testifying to it. She acknowledges the limits of the record in the Long Hall, ending with the guild's authority intact but no longer beyond scrutiny.","personality_traits":["Exacting","Proud","Protective","Ritual-minded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Map sealing","description":"Can authenticate registered star-maps and explain the safeguards governing their opening.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Institutional memory","description":"Knows the precedents and stakes behind the guild's sealing authority since the Map Wars.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_veska_dorn","name":"Veska Dorn","role":"supporting","description":"An Ice Baron who buys claims and tether rights ahead of each burn, Veska treats arbitration as another market in which timing matters more than sentiment. She has offered to fund Tovan's claim in exchange for future access to the route, though she frames the bargain as a way to keep indebted pilots from being stranded. Compact and silver-haired, she dresses in a dark mining coat with a tally of acquired claims stitched inside one cuff.","home_location_id":"loc_core_vaults","faction_id":"fac_ice_barons","motivation":"Turn the uncertainty before perihelion into enough secured claims to keep her holdings viable through the burn.","goal":"Gain leverage over the perihelion route and acquire tether rights from pilots unable to pay their ice-tithes.","flaw":"She reduces people and promises to assets, assuming a favorable contract can excuse the pressure behind it.","internal_conflict":"Veska wants to see herself as a steward of the comet's scarce resources, but her bargains often deepen the very dependence she claims to manage.","external_conflict":"The Tether Grab has made the Free Pilots' Compact wary of the Ice Barons, and her support for Tovan could be exposed as an attempt to profit from the chart dispute.","arc":"Veska begins believing that buying claims is simply what keeps the market orderly before a burn. When Mara's hearing connects her proposed route bargain to the pilots' lost tether rights, Veska must choose whether to press the deal or withdraw it publicly. She withdraws the offer in the Long Hall, ending with fewer immediate gains but a clearer boundary between investment and coercion.","personality_traits":["Pragmatic","Composed","Shrewd","Possessive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Claim valuation","description":"Quickly estimates the risks and leverage in ice claims, berth rights, and pre-burn contracts.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Hard bargaining","description":"Can negotiate complex exchanges while keeping her own concessions difficult to read.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tovan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tovan_reik","relationship_type":"arbiter and claimant","description":"Mara must judge Tovan's salvage claim; his candor or evasion can determine whether she sees him as a pilot defending a right or a trader exploiting a theft."},{"id":"rel_serit_mara","source_character_id":"chr_serit_oss","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"guild superior","description":"Serit trained Mara in registration work and expects her to protect the Mapmakers' Guild, creating pressure when Mara's audit complicates the guild's preferred ruling."},{"id":"rel_tovan_veska","source_character_id":"chr_tovan_reik","target_character_id":"chr_veska_dorn","relationship_type":"uneasy allies","description":"Veska offers backing for Tovan's claim in return for route access, while Tovan suspects her support is a way to acquire influence over the pilots' tethers."},{"id":"rel_serit_veska","source_character_id":"chr_serit_oss","target_character_id":"chr_veska_dorn","relationship_type":"rivals","description":"Serit sees Veska's claims-and-tethers strategy as a threat to a stable fleet, while Veska views the guild's control of sealed routes as a barrier to commerce."}]}
