ord to wait through another season. She grew up learning the value of shared obligations and carries herself with a directness that unsettles more ceremonious negotiators. Her travel cloak is practical and salt-faded, and she wears a small pepper-stained ledger pouch at her belt, guarded as carefully as any formal seal.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","motivation":"Keep her delegation's sailors and cargo from losing a season to delay or favoritism.","goal":"Have the court recognize her delegation's claim without allowing a rival to buy the decision.","flaw":"Her impatience makes her assume that cautious people are acting in bad faith.","internal_conflict":"She believes in collective duty but is tempted to secure a private advantage for her own delegation when the other claims remain uncertain.","external_conflict":"The three-way filing dispute and the discovery of unregistered gifts threaten both her claim and the court's ability to make a trusted ruling.","arc":"Mariyam begins treating every delay as evidence of corruption and presses for an immediate decision. When the gift-register rule makes clear that the scandal could taint any claim, she chooses to support Nila's public examination of the record instead of demanding a private advantage. She ends more willing to distinguish deliberate obstruction from the time required for a fair hearing.","personality_traits":["direct","energetic","loyal","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cargo accounting","description":"Can trace cargo obligations and identify which merchants bear the cost of a missed sailing season.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Persuasion","description":"Can rally her delegation around a shared risk and make its interests plain to the court.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas","name":"Tomas","role":"supporting","description":"Tomas is an envoy who has built his authority on anticipating what a rival will offer before the rival offers it. He has crossed many seasons of bargaining and knows tha