t a delayed fleet can cost more than a lost argument. His fine coat is kept immaculate despite the damp air, and the careful polish of his boots contrasts with the hurried state of the other delegations' travel gear.","home_location_id":"loc_envoy_house","motivation":"Keep his delegation's standing intact in a court where a lost slot could be remembered for years.","goal":"Win the first sailing slot or, failing that, prevent either rival from taking it through an unrecorded favor.","flaw":"He relies on leverage and insinuation so heavily that he makes honest cooperation difficult.","internal_conflict":"He wants a decision that the captains will respect but fears that appearing conciliatory will make him seem weak.","external_conflict":"His claim is entangled with the unregistered-gifts scandal, and his suspicion of the court makes it harder to distinguish evidence from accusation.","arc":"Tomas begins using suspicion as a shield, hinting that every rival may have purchased the slot. When Nila insists that the gift register be examined under the court's rule, he must choose whether to repeat an unsubstantiated accusation or put his own claim to the same scrutiny. He chooses scrutiny and ends able to bargain without treating every opponent as a conspirator.","personality_traits":["strategic","polished","competitive","wary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Bargaining","description":"Can anticipate concessions and frame proposals around the cost of delay.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_bhanu","name":"Bhanu","role":"supporting","description":"Bhanu is a master pilot who reads the sea from the harbour steps and takes part in the public declaration that the monsoon has turned. After the Ghat Oath, he learned that a pilot's authority depends on being witnessed as much as on being right. Weather-marked and broad-shouldered, he wears a simple wrap and carries the wooden staff used to steady himself on wet steps.","home_location_id":"loc_pilot_ghat","motivation":"Protect the ghat's public rite from the suspicion created when a pilot was once bought to misread the sea.","goal":"Declare the wind's turn only when the signs can be witnessed and defended before the harbour court.","flaw":"He hides behind procedure when a clear explanation might prevent others from distrusting his judgment.","internal_conflict":"He knows the ghat's authority requires both expertise and public trust, yet fears that explaining uncertainty will make people mistake caution for incompetence.","external_conflict":"The envoys' rival claims demand a sailing order before the season is lost, but the wind-law forbids departure until the ghat publicly declares the monsoon turned.","arc":"Bhanu begins relying on the rite's formality to keep questions at a distance. When the competing claims make the captains press him for a premature declaration, he chooses to explain his observations publicly and wait for the sea to justify the call. He ends still cautious, but willing to make his reasoning visible rather than asking the court to trust procedure alone.","personality_traits":["patient","weatherwise","reserved","conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Sea reading","description":"Can assess the wind and water conditions relevant to the public declaration at the pilot ghat.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Harbour piloting","description":"Knows the harbour approaches and the practical risks of sending vessels out under a changing monsoon.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_nila_rashid","source_character_id":"chr_nila","target_character_id":"chr_rashid","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Nila must test Rashid's first-slot claim against the ledger, while Rashid's guarded manner makes her suspect he is withholding evidence."},{"id":"rel_rashid_mariyam","source_character_id":"chr_rashid","target_character_id":"chr_mariyam","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Rashid and Mariyam both claim the first sailing slot, and each fears that the other's delegation will benefit from delay."},{"id":"rel_mariyam_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_mariyam","target_character_id":"chr_tomas","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mariyam distrusts Tomas's insinuations about purchased favors, while Tomas sees her urgency as an attempt to shut down scrutiny."},{"id":"rel_nila_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_nila","target_character_id":"chr_tomas","relationship_type":"adversary","description":"Nila's insistence on examining the gift register threatens Tomas's strategy of using suspicion as leverage."},{"id":"rel_nila_bhanu","source_character_id":"chr_nila","target_character_id":"chr_bhanu","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Nila needs Bhanu's public account of the wind-law's timing, while Bhanu needs the court's record to preserve trust in the ghat's declaration."}]}
