{"world_id":"wld_lantern_parish","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A newcomer to the parish, Mara has taken up the lamplighter's work at the Keeper's Croft after years of tending lamps in scattered farmsteads. She is spare, quick-handed, and keeps her hair bound beneath a wool cap; oil stains darken the cuffs of her coat. She accepted the post believing that steady work and exact records could make her useful in a place where nobody trusts an outsider. Her first winter on the wall brings her face to face with the cut page and the wardens' unwillingness to name the night it held.","home_location_id":"loc_keepers_croft","faction_id":"fac_lamp_wardens","motivation":"To prove she can keep the lamps burning without becoming complicit in a lie.","goal":"Find out which night was removed from the ledger and establish what happened to the wall's lights that night.","flaw":"She treats every uncertainty as a problem that can be solved by gathering more proof, even when delay puts people at risk.","internal_conflict":"Mara fears that accepting the wardens' judgment will make her part of their silence, but fears even more that acting without proof could bring the parish to ruin.","external_conflict":"The Lamp Wardens refuse to explain the missing page, while the Moot Council demands an account of the wall's oil and lit nights.","arc":"Mara begins determined to uncover the missing night before making any accusation. When the wall burns short and the council presses for an entry she cannot verify, she chooses to record the wardens' conflicting accounts beside the ledger rather than invent a clean answer or stay silent. She ends still uncertain of the whole truth, but willing to take responsibility for an honest record even when it makes her vulnerable to both factions.","personality_traits":["Observant","Tenacious","Reserved","Conscientious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wickwork","description":"Can trim, set, and tend wall lantern wicks so they burn steadily with limited oil.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Nightkeeping","description":"Remembers which lamps she has checked and notices small changes in their flame or oil level.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_eddan_crow","name":"Eddan Crow","role":"antagonist","description":"Eddan is the senior Lamp Warden, a narrow-shouldered man with a smoke-rough voice and a habit of carrying his wick knife even when the lamps are already lit. He has served the wall for most of his life and knows the old work by touch. Since the page was cut from the ledger, he has discouraged questions and insisted that the wardens' duty is to keep the lamps burning, not to invite the council into every failure. His years of service have made him respected among the wardens and increasingly feared by anyone who asks what that service has cost.","home_location_id":"loc_lantern_wall","faction_id":"fac_lamp_wardens","motivation":"To preserve the wall's vigil and the wardens' authority, which he believes are the parish's only defense against another Dark Winter.","goal":"Keep the missing night from becoming a public accusation that could divide the parish while the oil runs short.","flaw":"He mistakes control of information for protection and assumes others will make the same dangerous choices he would.","internal_conflict":"Eddan believes the wardens must answer for every lamp, yet cannot face what a truthful account of the missing night would say about his own judgment.","external_conflict":"Mara's questions and the council's demand for the ledger threaten to expose his role in keeping the cut page unexplained.","arc":"Eddan begins certain that silence is the safest way to preserve the wall. When Mara lays the wardens' contradictory accounts before him and refuses to enter a false lit night, he must choose between suppressing her record and admitting what he remembers. He gives his account to the council, ending with less control over the wardens' reputation but no longer making Mara carry his silence alone.","personality_traits":["Authoritative","Wary","Protective","Secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wallcraft","description":"Knows the wall's lantern fittings and can identify damage or tampering by sight and touch.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Warden's counsel","description":"Can command the attention of other wardens through years of service and hard-won standing.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tomas_wren","name":"Tomas Wren","role":"supporting","description":"Tomas is the Moot Council's ledger-keeper, a careful, ink-fingered man who sits beneath the church's dim windows and copies the parish's lit nights into a hand kept exact by long practice. He wears a patched dark coat and protects the ledger from damp as if its pages were themselves a wall. Tomas was taught that an unentered night did not happen; he has treated that rule as a duty rather than a question. The severed page has left him with an empty place in the book and a fear that the council's authority rests on a record he cannot defend.","home_location_id":"loc_moot_kirk","faction_id":"fac_moot_council","motivation":"To preserve the ledger as a trustworthy account of the parish rather than a tool for settling factional scores.","goal":"Learn what can be established about the missing night and keep the council from turning the oil dispute into a verdict without evidence.","flaw":"He hides behind procedure when a decision requires him to challenge people with greater standing.","internal_conflict":"Tomas wants the ledger to tell the truth, but has built his sense of safety around the belief that anything absent from it can be set aside.","external_conflict":"The council expects him to account for the missing page, while the wardens will not agree on what the ledger should say.","arc":"Tomas begins by treating the ledger's gap as a clerical problem he can contain. When Mara brings him the wardens' differing accounts, he chooses to preserve them as testimony beside the surviving entries rather than erase the uncertainty with a neat official version. He ends willing to let the council see that its record is incomplete, even though doing so weakens the authority he once thought the ledger guaranteed.","personality_traits":["Precise","Patient","Conflict-averse","Principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger hand","description":"Keeps clear, consistent records and can recognize alterations or gaps in a written account.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Measured inquiry","description":"Draws careful accounts from reluctant speakers by listening without immediately accusing them.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_ansa_fell","name":"Ansa Fell","role":"supporting","description":"Ansa is a turf-cutter whose family works the peat cuttings below the moor. Broad-handed and weather-browned, she wears a peat-dark shawl and keeps her small oil measure wrapped in cloth against the cold. She knows how quickly a poor cutting season can turn the oil tithe into a choice between the wall and a household's own needs. Ansa resents being blamed for the shortfall when the wardens' count seems to grow at every call-in, but she knows that a dark wall would not spare the cutters.","home_location_id":"loc_bog_hollow","faction_id":"fac_turf_cutters","motivation":"To keep her family from being made to answer for oil that never reached the wall.","goal":"Make the wardens and council account for their oil tally before the next midwinter call-in.","flaw":"Her anger at unfair demands makes her dismiss warnings from people she thinks serve the parish's powerful factions.","internal_conflict":"Ansa refuses to be frightened into obedience, yet fears that her refusal to yield oil could leave the wall dark and bring the bog's danger closer to everyone.","external_conflict":"The wardens accuse the turf-cutters of owing oil, while Ansa believes the wall burns short because the tally is wrong.","arc":"Ansa begins determined to withhold her oil until the wardens prove their count. When Mara arrives with no reliable entry for the night in question and the wall's oil store is dwindling, Ansa chooses to give a measured share while insisting that Tomas record exactly what she supplied. She ends still challenging the tithe, but no longer treats cooperation and surrender as the same thing.","personality_traits":["Blunt","Resourceful","Suspicious","Loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Peat reading","description":"Recognizes changes in the bog's footing and can judge which cuttings are safe to cross.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Fair measure","description":"Keeps close track of household stores and can spot when a tally does not match what was delivered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_eddan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara's insistence on accounting for the missing night challenges Eddan's belief that a warden must control what the parish knows."},{"id":"rel_eddan_mara","source_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Eddan taught Mara the wall's practical work, but his mentorship is strained by her refusal to accept his silence about the ledger."},{"id":"rel_mara_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara brings Tomas the wardens' conflicting accounts, and he helps her preserve them without pretending they settle the missing night."},{"id":"rel_ansa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ansa_fell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ansa sees Mara as a possible witness to the wardens' oil tally, while Mara needs Ansa's account of what the turf-cutters actually delivered."},{"id":"rel_ansa_eddan","source_character_id":"chr_ansa_fell","target_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ansa accuses Eddan and the wardens of over-counting the oil tithe; Eddan sees her refusal to pay without proof as a threat to the wall."},{"id":"rel_tomas_eddan","source_character_id":"chr_tomas_wren","target_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tomas needs the wardens to account for the cut page, while Eddan resents the council's demand to turn their night work into ledger entries."}]}
