unt. When Mara arrives with no reliable entry for the night in question and the wall's oil store is dwindling, Ansa chooses to give a measured share while insisting that Tomas record exactly what she supplied. She ends still challenging the tithe, but no longer treats cooperation and surrender as the same thing.","personality_traits":["Blunt","Resourceful","Suspicious","Loyal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Peat reading","description":"Recognizes changes in the bog's footing and can judge which cuttings are safe to cross.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Fair measure","description":"Keeps close track of household stores and can spot when a tally does not match what was delivered.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_eddan","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara's insistence on accounting for the missing night challenges Eddan's belief that a warden must control what the parish knows."},{"id":"rel_eddan_mara","source_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Eddan taught Mara the wall's practical work, but his mentorship is strained by her refusal to accept his silence about the ledger."},{"id":"rel_mara_tomas","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_tomas_wren","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara brings Tomas the wardens' conflicting accounts, and he helps her preserve them without pretending they settle the missing night."},{"id":"rel_ansa_mara","source_character_id":"chr_ansa_fell","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Ansa sees Mara as a possible witness to the wardens' oil tally, while Mara needs Ansa's account of what the turf-cutters actually delivered."},{"id":"rel_ansa_eddan","source_character_id":"chr_ansa_fell","target_character_id":"chr_eddan_crow","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ansa accuses Eddan an